# OCR Revamp: Google Cloud Vision + Gemini Text Parsing

Replace the current Gemini Vision-based OCR (which keeps hitting free tier quota) with a hybrid pipeline: **Google Cloud Vision API** for image-to-text extraction and **Gemini text-only** for smart structured parsing.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Google Cloud Setup Required** — You will need to enable the Cloud Vision API in your existing Google Cloud project and generate an API key. Detailed steps are provided below. No billing is required for the free tier (1,000 scans/month).

> [!WARNING]
> The current `/api/ocr` route and both scan handlers in `add-transaction-dialog.tsx` and `scan-receipt-dialog.tsx` will be fully rewritten. The old Gemini Vision approach will be completely removed.

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["📷 Camera"] --> B["Compress\n(client-side)"]
    B --> C["/api/ocr"]
    C --> D["Google Cloud\nVision API"]
    D --> E["Raw OCR Text"]
    E --> F{"Gemini\navailable?"}
    F -->|Yes| G["Gemini text-only\n~50 tokens"]
    F -->|No/Quota| H["Regex Fallback\nParser"]
    G --> I["Structured JSON"]
    H --> I
    I --> J["Pre-fill Form"]
```

### Why this is better

| | Old (Gemini Vision) | New (Vision API + Gemini text) |
|---|---|---|
| **Image OCR** | Gemini (shared quota) | Cloud Vision API (separate 1,000 free/mo) |
| **Tokens per scan** | ~2,000 (image) | ~50 (text only) |
| **Handwriting** | ✅ Good | ✅ Excellent (DOCUMENT_TEXT_DETECTION) |
| **Fallback** | ❌ None | ✅ Regex parser |
| **Cost at scale** | Expensive | ~₹0.10/scan after free tier |

